## Follow the runs in the function executions

![The Executions tab of the agent function with a short POST /runs execution, a longer POST /drain execution, and a schedule execution](/images/blog/ai-agent-live-collaborator-appwrite-presences/console-executions.avif)

The **Executions** tab of the `agent` function shows each part of a request. A short `POST /runs` execution queues the request, a longer `POST /drain` execution runs the agent, and a `schedule` execution runs every five minutes. The logs of a drain show the run ID, the kind of request, and how long the run took.

# Extend the agent with more tools

Each new ability is a tool and a row write, so the presence and Realtime code stay the same. Some tools that fit Weft:

- **Due dates.** `update_card` does not change `dueAt`. A `set_due_date` tool with a date in its schema lets the agent plan work toward the release date.
- **Comments.** A `comments` table with a `boardId` column and a `comment` tool let the agent ask a question on a card instead of guessing. Add the table to the Realtime subscription, and every comment appears on the board as the agent writes it.
- **Instructions for each board.** An `instructions` column on `boards`, added to the context message, lets each team tell the agent how it triages.

Keep each tool narrow, and check every argument in the function, as `update_card` does. Weft gives each kind of request only the tools it needs and has no tool that deletes cards. A new tool needs the same checks: the card is on the board, the team can read it, and every value is valid.

